{
  "<root>": "Tidy up your agent skills: find broken, duplicate and unused skills, and clear them out safely, with undo.\n\nUsage: skill-studio [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  invocation  Check invocation across copies, or set every copy of a skill\n  scan        List every skill installed for your agents\n  diagnose    Find broken skills and say what is wrong with each\n  conflicts   Find skills that have different copies in different places\n  review      Set, clear, or list skill review dates\n  library     Show library skills, their sources, uses, invocation modes and agent copies\n  pack        List, add, update, remove or switch the source of packs: one source that ships skills\n  recovery    List or drop interrupted writes that recovery cannot undo\n  usage       Show which skills your agents used in the last 30 days, and which they did not\n  park        Turn a skill off for all agents. You can turn it on again later\n  turn-off    Split a shared skill and park one agent's copy. Stops source updates for the copies\n  unpark      Turn a parked skill on again\n  enable      Same as `unpark`: turn a parked skill on again\n  disable     Same as `park`: turn a skill off for all agents\n  remove      Remove a skill. Copies you made go to a recovery folder\n  fix         Repair a skill's problems and list the ones it cannot repair\n  undo        Reverse your last change\n  events      List your past changes, newest first [alias: history]\n  restore     Reverse one change from your history\n  add         Install a skill for one or more agents\n  outdated    List skills that have an update\n  update      Update installed skills\n  mcp         Start the MCP server so an agent can tidy your skills\n  extras      List hook events, MCP server names, and instruction file paths. Writes nothing\n  listing     Show which skills each agent lists for the model with a description, with a name only, or not at all. This writes nothing\n  sessions    Show, per recent session, which skills were listed with a description, by name only, or not at all, which were used, and which were possibly missed. This writes nothing\n  doctor      Check skill state and model listing budgets. This writes nothing\n  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --time     Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help     Print help\n  -V, --version  Print version\n\nCommon questions:\n  Which library skills did I load most, and where did they come from?\n      skill-studio library --days 7 --sort uses --top 10 --json\n  Library uses = loads in the window, once per session; a sub-agent log is its own session; resumed or forked session copies and names no longer in the library do not count.\n  Fields: count = matching rows after scope and filters, before --top; name = skill; library = shared folder; agents = loads by agent; source null = not installed from a repo; modes = manual/auto; copies = link/same/old/changed.\n  Which skills are installed outside my library too?\n      skill-studio library --all --json\n  Which copies of a pack did not get the last update?\n      skill-studio library --source <owner/repo> --copy-status old --json\n  Which skills did I not use in the last 30 days?\n      skill-studio usage --json\n  How many library skills come from each source?\n      skill-studio library --count-by source --limit 0 --json\n  Which library skills does Claude Code read as manual and Codex as auto?\n      skill-studio library --mode claude-code=manual --mode codex=auto --fields name --json\n  Which skills do agents read in different modes?\n      skill-studio invocation --mismatches --json\n  What is broken?\n      skill-studio diagnose --json\nAdd --json for one JSON document. A long list returns one page; page.total counts every row and --cursor <page.next_cursor> gets the next one.",
  "add": "Install a skill for one or more agents\n\nUsage: skill-studio add [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>\n\nArguments:\n  <SOURCE>  Where the skill comes from: a repo such as owner/repo for skills-sh or dotagents, or a local folder for copy\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --method <METHOD>              How to install the skill [default: skills-sh] [possible values: copy, dotagents, skills-sh]\n      --agent <AGENT>                Agent to install for. Repeat for more than one: universal (the shared folder), claude-code, codex, opencode (alias open-code), cursor, pi or grok-build. Default: universal\n      --copy                         Put a real copy in each agent's folder, not a link to the shared copy\n      --global                       Install for your user account. This is the default\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Install into this project instead of for your user account\n      --name <NAME>                  Folder name for the skill. Needed for skills-sh and dotagents: it is the skill's name in the repo. For copy, the default is the source folder's name\n      --trust                        Trust a dotagents source you have not used before\n      --json                         Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "apply-repair": "Apply a previously-previewed frontmatter repair\n\nUsage: skill-studio apply-repair [OPTIONS] --preview-json <PREVIEW_JSON>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --preview-json <PREVIEW_JSON>  Preview envelope, as printed by `preview-repair --json` (its `.data` field)\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "capabilities": "Report harness capability facts\n\nUsage: skill-studio capabilities [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                 Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>          Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>   Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --harness <HARNESSES>  Restrict to these harnesses\n      --observe              Also probe the machine (config presence, runner binary)\n      --tool <TOOLS>         Executables to look up on `PATH`\n      --json                 \n  -h, --help                 Print help",
  "conflicts": "Find skills that have different copies in different places\n\nUsage: skill-studio conflicts [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "diagnose": "Find broken skills and say what is wrong with each\n\nUsage: skill-studio diagnose [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILLS>      Only check this skill. Repeat for more than one\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "disable": "Same as `park`: turn a skill off for all agents\n\nUsage: skill-studio disable [OPTIONS] [SKILLS]...\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILLS]...  Names of the skills to change\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by scan\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "doctor": "Check skill state and model listing budgets. This writes nothing\n\nUsage: skill-studio doctor [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "enable": "Same as `unpark`: turn a parked skill on again\n\nUsage: skill-studio enable [OPTIONS] [SKILLS]...\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILLS]...  Names of the skills to change\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by scan\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "events": "List your past changes, newest first\n\nUsage: skill-studio events [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILL>       Only show changes to this skill\n      --limit <LIMIT>       Most changes to show. 0 shows the default number [default: 0]\n      --after <AFTER>       Only show changes older than this one. Use an id from this list\n      --check-drift         Also check which files changed after each change\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "extras": "List hook events, MCP server names, and instruction file paths. Writes nothing\n\nUsage: skill-studio extras [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "fix": "Repair a skill's problems and list the ones it cannot repair\n\nUsage: skill-studio fix [OPTIONS] --skill <SKILL>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILL>       Skill to fix\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "harnesses": "Detect first-class harnesses installed on this machine: `PATH`, version, install method, configured, and used evidence\n\nUsage: skill-studio harnesses [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "health": "Print the command health rollup: count, failures, p50/p95 duration, and last error, per command, over the last 7 days of `timing.jsonl`\n\nUsage: skill-studio health [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                     Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --timing-log <TIMING_LOG>  Path to the timing log to read. Defaults to the desktop app's own `timing.jsonl` (its app data dir, resolved through `dirs` - the same file the desktop's Settings \"Command health\" card reads via its own Tauri command)\n      --json                     \n  -h, --help                     Print help",
  "install-preferences": "Print the method and harnesses the next `add` pre-selects: the last install's saved preference, or the environment default when nothing has been saved for this scope yet\n\nUsage: skill-studio install-preferences [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Project whose preference to read; omit for the scope home's. Named `--project-path` for the same reason `add`'s flag is: `ScopeArgs` already flattens a repeatable `--project`\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "invocation": "Check invocation across copies, or set every copy of a skill\n\nUsage: skill-studio invocation [OPTIONS] [SKILL]\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILL]  \n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --manual              \n      --auto                \n      --mismatches          Only list skills that agents read in different modes\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "library": "Show library skills, their sources, uses, invocation modes and agent copies\n\nUsage: skill-studio library [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --all                        Include skills outside ~/.agents/skills\n      --time                       Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --source <SOURCE>            Only show this owner/repo, plugin@marketplace, or manual\n      --skill <SKILLS>             Only show this skill. Repeat for more than one\n      --copy-status <COPY_STATUS>  Only show rows with this agent copy status: link, same, old, changed\n      --home <HOME>                Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>         Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --days <DAYS>                How many days back to count uses, 30 at most [default: 30]\n      --since <SINCE>              Count uses from this date (YYYY-MM-DD or RFC 3339), 30 days ago at the earliest\n      --until <UNTIL>              Count uses before this date (YYYY-MM-DD or RFC 3339)\n      --sort <SORT>                Order rows by name or uses [possible values: name, uses]\n      --top <TOP>                  Show only the N most used skills\n      --mode <AGENT=MODE>          Only show rows that this agent reads in this mode: AGENT=manual or AGENT=auto. Repeat for more than one agent\n      --limit <N>                  Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>            Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>            Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>           Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                       Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                       Print help",
  "listing": "Show which skills each agent lists for the model with a description, with a name only, or not at all. This writes nothing\n\nUsage: skill-studio listing [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time\n          Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>\n          Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>\n          Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>\n          Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>\n          Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>\n          Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>\n          Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --for-project <FOR_PROJECT>\n          Also show this project's sessions. It must be in the scope\n      --claude-fraction <CLAUDE_FRACTION>\n          Predict Claude Code at this `skillListingBudgetFraction`, for example 0.02\n      --claude-context <CLAUDE_CONTEXT>\n          Predict Claude Code with this context window, in tokens\n      --codex-max-tokens <CODEX_MAX_TOKENS>\n          Predict Codex at this `skills.max_context_tokens`\n      --claude-session <CLAUDE_SESSION>\n          Compare Claude Code with this session transcript (.jsonl) instead of the newest one\n      --codex-session <CODEX_SESSION>\n          Compare Codex with this session rollout (rollout-*.jsonl) instead of the newest one\n      --json\n          \n  -h, --help\n          Print help",
  "mcp": "Start the MCP server so an agent can tidy your skills\n\nUsage: skill-studio mcp [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time  Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help  Print help",
  "outdated": "List skills that have an update\n\nUsage: skill-studio outdated [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILLS>      Only check this skill. Repeat for more than one\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "pack": "List, add, update, remove or switch the source of packs: one source that ships skills\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  list           List every installed pack. Reads local files only unless --remote is given\n  show           Show the packs with one source, as pack list prints it\n  add            Install the skills of one git pack with npx skills add\n  update         Update the skills of one pack, or of every pack with --all. Skips skills with local edits\n  remove         Remove the skills of one pack. Skips skills with local edits\n  switch-source  Install the skills of one skills.sh pack from another git source, such as your fork, and keep the old source as the pack's original. pack show <to> --remote then compares the two. Skips skills with local edits\n  export         Copy installed skills into a new folder laid out as a pack: skills/<name>/ for each and a README with the install lines. Push the folder to git and anyone can install it with npx skills add. Writes nothing else and never overwrites a file\n  help           Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --time  Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help  Print help",
  "pack add": "Install the skills of one git pack with npx skills add\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack add [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>\n\nArguments:\n  <SOURCE>  owner/repo or a git URL\n\nOptions:\n      --skill <SKILL>                Skill to install. Repeat for more than one. Default: every skill of the pack that is not installed yet, read with git\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --ref <REF>                    Branch, tag or commit to pin the pack to\n      --agent <AGENT>                Agent to install for, as in add. Repeat for more than one. Default: universal (the shared folder)\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project. For add: install into this project\n      --dry-run                      Print the plan and change nothing\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack export": "Copy installed skills into a new folder laid out as a pack: skills/<name>/ for each and a README with the install lines. Push the folder to git and anyone can install it with npx skills add. Writes nothing else and never overwrites a file\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack export [OPTIONS] --skill <SKILL> <DIR>\n\nArguments:\n  <DIR>  New or empty folder to create the pack in\n\nOptions:\n      --skill <SKILL>                Skill to put in the pack. Repeat for more than one\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --source <SOURCE>              Where the pack will live, as owner/repo or a git URL, for the README's install lines. Default: <owner>/<repo>\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project. For add: install into this project\n      --dry-run                      Print the plan and change nothing\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack list": "List every installed pack. Reads local files only unless --remote is given\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack list [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project\n      --remote                       Ask each git source for its newest commit and skills\n      --limit <N>                    Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>              Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>              Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>             Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack remove": "Remove the skills of one pack. Skips skills with local edits\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack remove [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>\n\nArguments:\n  <SOURCE>  Pack source, as pack list prints it\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project. For add: install into this project\n      --dry-run                      Print the plan and change nothing\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack show": "Show the packs with one source, as pack list prints it\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack show [OPTIONS] <SOURCE>\n\nArguments:\n  <SOURCE>  \n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project\n      --remote                       Ask each git source for its newest commit and skills\n      --limit <N>                    Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>              Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>              Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>             Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack switch-source": "Install the skills of one skills.sh pack from another git source, such as your fork, and keep the old source as the pack's original. pack show <to> --remote then compares the two. Skips skills with local edits\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack switch-source [OPTIONS] <SOURCE> <TO>\n\nArguments:\n  <SOURCE>  Pack source, as pack list prints it\n  <TO>      owner/repo or a git URL to install from instead; add #ref to pin a branch or tag\n\nOptions:\n      --skill <SKILL>                Skill to move. Repeat for more than one. Default: every skill of the pack\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project. For add: install into this project\n      --dry-run                      Print the plan and change nothing\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "pack update": "Update the skills of one pack, or of every pack with --all. Skips skills with local edits\n\nUsage: skill-studio pack update [OPTIONS] [SOURCE]\n\nArguments:\n  [SOURCE]  Pack source, as pack list prints it\n\nOptions:\n      --all                          Update every installed pack\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Only this project. For add: install into this project\n      --dry-run                      Print the plan and change nothing\n      --json                         \n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "park": "Turn a skill off for all agents. You can turn it on again later\n\nUsage: skill-studio park [OPTIONS] [SKILLS]...\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILLS]...  Names of the skills to change\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by scan\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "preview-repair": "Preview a frontmatter repair for one deployment, without writing\n\nUsage: skill-studio preview-repair [OPTIONS] --deployment-id <DEPLOYMENT_ID>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                           Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                    Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>             Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --deployment-id <DEPLOYMENT_ID>  Deployment to repair\n      --json                           \n  -h, --help                           Print help",
  "recovery": "List or drop interrupted writes that recovery cannot undo\n\nUsage: skill-studio recovery [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  list  List the plans that block writes, with the paths each one may have left half done\n  drop  Give up one interrupted plan, so writes run again. Changes no file the plan touched: check those paths by hand. This cannot be undone\n  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --time  Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help  Print help",
  "recovery drop": "Give up one interrupted plan, so writes run again. Changes no file the plan touched: check those paths by hand. This cannot be undone\n\nUsage: skill-studio recovery drop [OPTIONS] <PLAN_ID>\n\nArguments:\n  <PLAN_ID>  Plan ID, as recovery list prints it\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "recovery list": "List the plans that block writes, with the paths each one may have left half done\n\nUsage: skill-studio recovery list [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>           Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>     Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>     Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>    Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "remove": "Remove a skill. Copies you made go to a recovery folder\n\nUsage: skill-studio remove [OPTIONS] [SKILL]\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILL]  Name of the skill\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by `scan`. Use it when the name matches more than one copy\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "restore": "Reverse one change from your history\n\nUsage: skill-studio restore [OPTIONS] --event-id <EVENT_ID>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                 Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>          Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>   Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --event-id <EVENT_ID>  Change to reverse, as printed by `events`\n      --force                Reverse it even if the files changed after it\n      --json                 Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                 Print help",
  "review": "Set, clear, or list skill review dates\n\nUsage: skill-studio review [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  set    Set a review date in YYYY-MM-DD form\n  clear  Clear a saved review date\n  due    List skills with a review date before today in UTC\n  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n      --time  Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help  Print help",
  "review clear": "Clear a saved review date\n\nUsage: skill-studio review clear [OPTIONS] <SKILL>\n\nArguments:\n  <SKILL>  \n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "review due": "List skills with a review date before today in UTC\n\nUsage: skill-studio review due [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "review set": "Set a review date in YYYY-MM-DD form\n\nUsage: skill-studio review set [OPTIONS] <SKILL> <DATE>\n\nArguments:\n  <SKILL>  \n  <DATE>   \n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "scan": "List every skill installed for your agents\n\nUsage: skill-studio scan [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --source <SOURCE>            Only show skills from this owner/repo, plugin@marketplace, or manual\n      --time                       Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --root <ROOT>                Only show skills in ~/.agents/skills [possible values: library]\n      --copy-status <COPY_STATUS>  Only show agent copies with this status against the library copy: link, same, differs or stale (older than the last update)\n      --home <HOME>                Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>         Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILLS>             Only show this skill. Repeat for more than one\n      --limit <N>                  Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>            Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>            Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>           Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --json                       Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                       Print help",
  "schema": "Write one JSON Schema file per request/result DTO\n\nUsage: skill-studio schema [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --out <OUT>  Directory to write schema files into\n      --time       Print how long each step took, to stderr\n  -h, --help       Print help",
  "sessions": "Show, per recent session, which skills were listed with a description, by name only, or not at all, which were used, and which were possibly missed. This writes nothing\n\nUsage: skill-studio sessions [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                       Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>         Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --limit <N>                  Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n      --cursor <CURSOR>            Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n      --fields <FIELDS>            Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n      --count-by <FIELD>           Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n      --for-project <FOR_PROJECT>  Only this project's sessions. It must be in the scope\n      --sessions <SESSIONS>        Newest sessions to read per agent (default 100, at most 500)\n      --json                       \n  -h, --help                       Print help",
  "split": "Replace a Universal skill folder with one real copy per chosen harness. Harnesses not named lose the skill\n\nUsage: skill-studio split [OPTIONS] --deployment-id <DEPLOYMENT_ID> --harness <HARNESSES>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                           Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                    Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>             Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --deployment-id <DEPLOYMENT_ID>  Universal deployment to split, as printed by `scan`\n      --harness <HARNESSES>            A harness that keeps the skill. Repeat for more than one\n      --json                           \n  -h, --help                           Print help",
  "sweep-quarantine": "Prune the global quarantine cap without a `remove` call, via `ops::sweep_quarantine`. Global scope only - see that function's own doc\n\nUsage: skill-studio sweep-quarantine [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "turn-off": "Split a shared skill and park one agent's copy. Stops source updates for the copies\n\nUsage: skill-studio turn-off [OPTIONS] --agent <AGENT> [SKILL]\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILL]  Name of the skill\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by `scan`. Use it when the name matches more than one copy\n      --agent <AGENT>       \n      --check               Preview refusals and git status without changing files\n      --confirm             Confirm the split and park after reviewing --check\n      --json                \n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "undo": "Reverse your last change\n\nUsage: skill-studio undo [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --force               Reverse it even if the files changed after it\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "unpark": "Turn a parked skill on again\n\nUsage: skill-studio unpark [OPTIONS] [SKILLS]...\n\nArguments:\n  [SKILLS]...  Names of the skills to change\n\nOptions:\n      --time                Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>         Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>  Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --id <ID>             Id of one copy, as printed by scan\n      --json                Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                Print help",
  "update": "Update installed skills\n\nUsage: skill-studio update [OPTIONS] --skill <SKILLS> --method <METHOD>\n\nOptions:\n      --time                         Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>                  Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>           Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --skill <SKILLS>               Skill to update. Repeat for more than one\n      --method <METHOD>              How the skill was installed [possible values: copy, dotagents, skills-sh]\n      --project-path <PROJECT_PATH>  Project the skill is in. Leave it out for your global skills\n      --source-dir <SOURCE_DIR>      For copy: the folder to read the new files from\n      --source <SOURCE>              For skills-sh or dotagents: where to get the skill again, such as owner/repo\n      --ref-pin <REF_PIN>            For dotagents: the commit to update to\n      --json                         Print the result as JSON\n  -h, --help                         Print help",
  "usage": "Show which skills your agents used in the last 30 days, and which they did not.\n\nUses = loads in the window, once per session; a sub-agent log is its own session; resumed or forked session copies and names no longer in the library do not count.\n\nUsage: skill-studio usage [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --harness <AGENT>\n          Keep uses from this agent id only\n\n      --time\n          Print how long each step took, to stderr\n\n      --home <HOME>\n          Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n\n      --project <PROJECTS>\n          Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n\n      --days <DAYS>\n          How many days back to count uses, 30 at most\n          \n          [default: 30]\n\n      --since <SINCE>\n          Count uses from this date (YYYY-MM-DD or RFC 3339) instead of --days, 30 days ago at the earliest\n\n      --until <UNTIL>\n          Count uses before this date (YYYY-MM-DD or RFC 3339)\n\n      --top <N>\n          Show only the N most used skills\n\n      --limit <N>\n          Print at most N rows of the main list; 0 prints only the totals\n\n      --cursor <CURSOR>\n          Continue with an opaque `next_cursor`. Repeat the same scope and filters\n\n      --fields <FIELDS>\n          Keep only these row fields, comma-separated\n\n      --count-by <FIELD>\n          Count all rows by this field, in page.counts\n\n      --json\n          Print the result as JSON\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')",
  "watch": "Stream one JSON line per revision change: an initial line with the current revision and inventory, then one line per change, until interrupted or `--max-seconds` passes\n\nUsage: skill-studio watch [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n      --time                   Print how long each step took, to stderr\n      --home <HOME>            Use this folder as the home folder instead of yours\n      --project <PROJECTS>     Project folder to include. Repeat for more than one. Without it, Skill Studio finds your projects for you\n      --since <SINCE>          Suppress the initial full line when the current revision already equals this one\n      --max-seconds <SECONDS>  Stop after this many seconds and exit 0. Leave it out to watch until Ctrl-C\n      --json                   \n  -h, --help                   Print help"
}
